---
// The Lumit wordmark, assembled on load out of the app mark.
//
// The mark reads as two chevrons either side of a white core. A chevron and an L
// are both six-cornered outlines with matching corners, so this is a real `d`
// morph rather than a crossfade: the same path thins from the icon's keyframe
// into the letter while it flies out and turns 45 degrees anti-clockwise. Nothing
// fades or is swapped, and each keeps its icon gradient throughout.
//
// The t is the L rotated 180 degrees — which is free, because ">" is "<" rotated
// 180, so the same turn and the same morph land it upside down on their own. Its
// arm overhangs the deliberately dotless i, standing in for both tittle and t.
//
// "umi" is outlined from the same font the site ships, so the logotype cannot
// drift from the body text. The `d` attributes in the markup hold the FINISHED
// shapes, so a browser that cannot animate `d` shows the completed wordmark.
interface Props { class?: string }
const { class: klass } = Astro.props;
---

<svg class:list={["wm", klass]} viewBox="-14 -92 289 106" role="img" aria-label="Lumit" fill="none">
